<title>CHINA: China's Qinghai issues 40 mln yuan power bonds.</title>
<headline>China's Qinghai issues 40 mln yuan power bonds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's northwestern Qinghai province has launched an issue of 40 million yuan ($4.8 million) worth of power bonds from 10 May, the Financial News said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bonds, with two years maturity, carry an annual interest rate of 10.2 percent, it said.</p>
<p>Funds raised would be used for construction of the Li Jiaxia hydropower station and expansion of the fifth phase of the Qinghai Qiaotou power plant, it said.</p>
<p>($1.0 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
